meta {
  name: List Products
  type: http
  seq: 2
}

get {
  url: {{pim_base_url_v3}}/products?_fields=sku&_fields=status
  body: none
  auth: none
}

headers {
  Authorization: Bearer {{access_token}}
  Accept: application/json
}

assert {
  res.status: eq 200
  res.body.data: isArray
  res.body.pagination: isDefined
}

docs {
  Confirmed live 2026-09-04 against "David's Dev Account" (see
  `02-Products-v3/Get Access Token (Dev).bru`, in this same folder so a
  folder-level `bru run "02-Products-v3/" --env "Dev"` covers both without
  mixing in the Sandbox-only requests in `01-Authentication/`). Run with
  `--env "Dev"`, after running that auth request first to populate
  `access_token`.

  ## What it does
  `GET /api/v3/products` with repeated `_fields` query params to select a
  sparse field set, exactly as described by Plytix and by `API V3.md`'s
  `_fields` section. Matches `openapi_pimv3.json`'s `SearchProductsResponse`
  schema exactly: top-level `data` (array of product objects), `errors`
  (array, empty on success), `pagination` (object with `next_page`, a full
  URL for the next page -- confirms cursor/page-link style pagination, not
  offset/limit params).

  ## This resolves the v3-unreachable blocker
  v3 is live and matches its documented shape. It was unreachable earlier
  only because it was tested against the wrong host/account
  (`pim.plytix.com` under the "API Docs" account) -- v3 for this engagement
  is served from a separate DEV host/account. See
  `config/api-testing.config.md` for the full history.

  ## Spec discrepancy found
  `openapi_pimv3.json`'s `GET /api/v3/products` operation declares **zero**
  query parameters -- no `_fields`, no pagination params. But `_fields`
  demonstrably works live exactly as documented in `API V3.md` (the prose
  doc, not the spec). Per this repo's trust order (verified live behavior >
  raw materials > spec for *behavior*, but spec > prose for *shapes* where
  they conflict) -- here they don't conflict on shape, only on
  completeness: the spec is simply missing parameters that exist and work.
  Flag to Plytix: `openapi_pimv3.json`'s parameter list for this endpoint
  (and possibly others) is incomplete/stale relative to the real API.
}
